# CROSS-REFERENCED against EkagraTheBeast/reinforced-shulker-boxes@26.2,
# which discovered (via reflection, not an access widener) that cauldron
# interaction registration now goes through a private
# CauldronInteraction.Dispatcher.put(Item, CauldronInteraction) method
# instead of the old 1.21.11 public
# CauldronBehavior.WATER_CAULDRON_BEHAVIOR.put(...) map. Rather than copy
# their reflection-based workaround, this port widens the method directly
# -- consistent with how this project already solves every other
# visibility problem. CONFIRMED against the actual 26.1.2 jar and verified
# in-game (cauldron undyeing works correctly).
accessible method net/minecraft/core/cauldron/CauldronInteraction$Dispatcher put (Lnet/minecraft/world/item/Item;Lnet/minecraft/core/cauldron/CauldronInteraction;)V

